For once in her life Gertie Pye made all the sensation she desired. If she had thrown a bomb among the complacent Improvers she could hardly have made more.

" It can't be true," said Anne blankly.

" That's just what / said when I heard it first, d'on't you know," said Gertie, who was enjoying herself hugely. " / said it couldn't be true . . . that Judson Parker wouldn't have the heart to do it, don't you

